[ChapterName "5. Nxe2 Qxa2 (6. Qxe8 Qxa1 variation)"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/f3NuTHGo/AzMsB6DD"]
[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/Dy1ar"]
[FEN "rn2kbnr/ppp1pppp/8/3q4/Q7/8/PP1PNP1P/RNB1KB1R b - - 0 5"]
[SetUp "1"]
[UTCDate "2025.11.19"]
[UTCTime "04:00:54"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ As soon as black plays Qxa2, it's a loss. The lines can get complicated, but rely on your confidence that you have already won. The Qxa2 lines aren't that difficult to remember. } { [%cal Gd5a2] }
5... Qxa2 6. Qxe8 Qxa1 { We're going in order from left to right: Qxa1, Qxb1, Qxb2. Those are black's three possible moves here. This one is easiest. } (6... Qxb2 7. Qxf7 Qxb1 8. Rxa7 Qxc1 9. Nxc1 Rxa7 10. Qxg7 Bxg7 11. Na2 Rxa2 12. d4) 7. Qxb8 { The most popular move for white here is to blow the win by taking on f7. Here's a shorthand to remember this correct move: if the black queen "runs away" into the corner, "chase it" by taking the piece closest to it. That's the knight on b8. } (7. Qxf7 { This move blows the forced win for white. White's chances are still good, but now it's a queen race where black has a chance. }) (7. Qxe7 { This move blows the forced win for white. White's chances are still good, but now it's a queen race where black has a chance. }) 7... Qxb1 { Qxb1 is black's best move. The other possible moves are shown in the two quizzes in the chapters that follow this one--they're pretty easy wins for white. This one is slightly harder. } 8. Qxa7 { This is actually the only move that maintains the forced win for white. } 8... Rxa7 { Things start to get a little tricky here. If the queen had taken on b2 or c1 instead of Rxa7, it's an easy win for white--you just recapture the queen. See if you can find white's next move! } 9. Rg1 { That's a tough one to remember. If you've made it this far, though, you can close the deal. This is really the only tricky move for white. Just remember: If you can't find a way to punish that queen, maybe you need to play another piece. Keep in mind that you've already won. Do not play a fearful, defensive move. Black can't do anything to you. Be aggressive. Black only has two moves here, and neither are good. You know what to do next. } 9... Qxb2 { If black takes the bishop, you play the same next move. } 10. Rxg7 { Ahh, what is black to do? Nothing, that's what. It's over quickly from here! } 10... Qxc1 11. Nxc1 Bxg7 12. d4 Bxd4 { There are several ways to finish things off from here. } 13. Kd1 Bxf2 14. h4 Bxh4 15. Na2 Rxa2 16. Kc2 Rxc2 17. Be2 Rxe2# *


