[ChapterName "5. Nxe2 Qxd2 (6. Qxe8 Qxb2 7. Qxf8 Qxb1 variation)"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/f3NuTHGo/LWJ9pieS"]
[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/Dy1ar"]
[FEN "rn3Qnr/ppp1pppp/8/8/8/8/Pq2NP1P/RNB1KB1R b - - 0 7"]
[SetUp "1"]
[UTCDate "2025.11.25"]
[UTCTime "03:02:42"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ In this line, black is going to play Qxb1 instead of Qxe2 (which we covered in the previous chapter). } { [%cal Gb2b1] }
7... Qxb1 8. Qxg7 { If the black queen takes on the a file, it's over quickly. I'll make this into a quiz in the next chapter so you can work through it. Black's only real choice here is Qxc1. } { [%cal Gb1c1] } 8... Qxc1 9. Qxh7 { Black is in a tough spot here. Taking anything with the queen will allow white to release the h-file rook. The only decent option is to take the rook, which initiates a rook race. } 9... Rxh7 (9... Qxa1 10. Qxg8 Qxe1 11. Qxb8 Qxf2 12. Qxc7 Qxh2 13. Rxh2 Rxh2 14. Qxb7 Rxe2 15. Qxa7 Rxa7 16. Bxe2 Rxa2 17. Ba6 Rxa6#) 10. Rxc1 Rxh2 11. Rxc7 Rxf2 12. Rxb7 Rxe2 13. Kxe2 { This is clearly a difficult move to find. Notice that white's rook must be captured, whether it takes on a7 or e7. What if black plays Nh6? No good. White plays Rxa7, releasing black's rook. The only move that avoids immediate loss is a6. } { [%cal Ga7a6] } (13. Rxa7 Rxe1 14. Rxa8 Rxf1 15. Rxb8 Rxh1 16. Rxg8 Rh5 17. Rh8 Rxh8 18. a4 Rh6 19. a5 Rh5 20. a6 Rc5 21. a7 Rd5 22. a8=K) 13... a6 14. Rxe7 Nxe7 { Opening up the white bishop looks tempting... } 15. Kd3 { That's the move. The idea is that white wants to avoid a situation where the bishop takes on a6 and then black takes back with the knight, making it difficult for white to get rid of the a pawn. } 15... f6 16. Kc3 { Yes! That's the right move no matter what black plays: f6, f5, any knight move (except if he moves the knight on b8, which would be an immediate win for white with Rh8), Ra7, or a5. Any move black makes, just open up that bishop. } 16... f5 17. Bxa6 Nxa6 18. Kb4 Nxb4 19. a3 Rxa3 20. Ra1 Rxa1# *


[Event "Let's Learn the Wizard Opening - antichess: Quiz: find the win"]
