{ This time, black plays Qxe1. This is the most commonly played move, and black's idea is just to keep the queen race going until he finds an opportunity. } { [%cal Gd2e1] }
6... Qxe1 7. Qxf7 { Heading to the safe space. It's a win in 21 for white. Things might look dangerous for white, but you're good. The most common move by far for black, Qxf2, is a loss in 10. See if you can figure it out in the next chapter's quiz. Qxf1 is also a quick win, thought a tiny bit harder to find. I'll make that a quiz as well. Black's only hope is Qxe2! } { [%cal Ge1e2] } 7... Qxe2 8. Bxe2 { We've been here before: both bishops looking dangerous, but with our queen in black's territory we are still in control. } 8... b5 9. Bxb5 Nd7 10. Bxd7 { Black's best move is e6. It doesn't look so great, and that's because it's not. } { [%cal Ge7e6] } 10... e6 11. Bxe6 Rd8 12. Qxg7 Bxg7 13. Bxg8 Bxb2 14. Bxb2 Rdxg8 15. Bxh8 Rxh8 16. Rd1 Rd8 17. Rxd8 { This cleanup shouldn't be too difficult. } 17... a5 18. Nd2 c5 19. Rd4 cxd4 20. a4 d3 21. Re1 h5 22. Re2 dxe2 23. h4 e1=B 24. Nf1 Bxf2 25. Ng3 Bxg3# *


